Package: wordmood
Type: Package
Title: Simple Word-Based Sentiment Scoring for Text Files
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Manuel", "Pinto", email = "mmpinto73@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Counts positive and negative words in a text document and
    summarises the result as counts, a ratio, a balance score and a label.
    Word lists can use a wildcard (*) as prefix or suffix, so that "nause*"
    matches both "nauseous" and "nauseated", and every pattern can carry a
    confidence weight between 0 and 1. Negation is handled: a positive
    word shortly after "not", "never" or "don't" (as in "not very happy")
    counts as negative. Only base R is required.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports: utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
